invariant: INV-14
file: srv_auth.c
catches: srv_tcp_nonblocking_test
reason: key_lengths_match stops bounding an RSA slot's pub_len, so a
  server takes a modulus length longer than the SRV_SIG_MAX bytes its
  flight signs into, and srv_sign_certificate_verify refuses it with
  CH_ECAP after the ServerHello went out. bin/srv_tcp_nonblocking_test
  requires SRV_SIG_MAX + 1 to be refused at ch_srv_record_init with
  nothing sent.

--- old
    return id->priv_len == sizeof(ch_rsa_priv) && id->pub_len <= SRV_SIG_MAX;
--- new
    return id->priv_len == sizeof(ch_rsa_priv);
